From: PS4 Linux Baikal Port <noreply@ps4-linux>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/ps4: adapt bridge attach callback to Linux 6.18

Linux 6.18 passes the encoder explicitly to drm_bridge_funcs.attach.
The PS4 bridge has no attach-time work, so accept the argument and keep
the existing no-op behavior.

Upstream API reference:
https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git/tree/include/drm/drm_bridge.h?h=v6.18.44

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c
@@ -910,6 +910,7 @@ enum drm_mode_status ps4_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_connector *connector,
 }
 
 static int ps4_bridge_attach(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
+                             struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 			     enum drm_bridge_attach_flags flags)
 {
 	/* struct ps4_bridge *mn_bridge = bridge_to_ps4_bridge(bridge); */
